# Figure notebooks

## Purpose

Someone should be able to clone this repo, run a notebook top to bottom, and
recreate the published panel. Prefer simple, readable panel code over clever
abstractions.

## Fidelity

- Match the submitted / original publication plots unless the user directs a
  change. Assume the prior analysis and styling were correct; do not
  “improve” plot type, aggregation, colors, limits, or labels on your own.
- If the destination already has panel letters but wrong visuals (e.g. bars
  instead of the original histograms), treat that as incomplete migration, not
  an intentional redesign.
- Keep reported statistics identical to the source analysis unless a specific
  error is identified and confirmed.

## Structure

- Name main figures `figNN.ipynb` and supplements `suppSN.ipynb`.
- Start with: manuscript figure heading, full-composite image, code heading,
  one-sentence goal, panel/input map, and explicit output filenames.
- Follow with an imports-only cell and an optional shared-settings cell.
- Put shared RC / `sns.set_context` once in imports or the settings cell—never
  wrap every panel in the same `with sns.plotting_context(...)`.
- **DPI 300 for all figures.** In the imports cell call
  `configure_publication_dpi()` (from `violations_glm.plotting`). Do not set a
  different `dpi=` on `plt.subplots` / `Figure` unless matching 300. Saved PNGs
  go through `save_figure`, which defaults to `FIGURE_DPI = 300`.
- Use one markdown heading plus one code cell per panel.
- Import loaders, transforms, statistics, and shared plots from
  `violations_glm`; do not manipulate `sys.path`.
- Do not fit models in notebooks. Load stable summaries produced by scripts.
- Do not read files with bare relative strings. Use named package loaders.
- Keep panel-specific layout, labels, reference lines, and narrative comments
  in the notebook; keep aggregation and stats in the package.
- Use `save_figure` with stems such as `fig03a_violation_autocorrelation`.
- Do not call `plt.close()`; let figures display inline.
- Avoid function definitions unless under five lines and used once.
- Remove scratch/debug cells (`foo?`, exploratory plots) and clear outputs
  before committing.
- Notebooks must execute top to bottom in a fresh kernel. After editing
  package exports (`config`, loaders, transforms), restart the kernel before
  re-running imports.

## Panel moves and verification

- When moving a panel between figures/supplements, renumber letters and
  `save_figure` stems together and update `scripts/verify_cached.py` in the
  same change.
- Record value-affecting or placement changes in `REVISION.md` and migration
  status in `MIGRATION.md`.
